    "title": "Zendaya and Tom Holland Are Married, Stylist Law Roach Says",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTThe subject was brought up during the Actor Awards, to which Zendaya’s longtime stylist replied, “It’s very true.”Listen · 3:14 min Husband and wife?Credit...Emma McIntyre/Getty ImagesMarch 2, 2026Without being nominated, or even attending, Zendaya and Tom Holland still managed to be the subjects of one of the biggest stories coming out of the Actor Awards presented by SAG-AFTRA. Did they get married?Zendaya’s stylist, Law Roach, appears to have casually revealed that they did.After an “Access Hollywood” reporter asked him about Zendaya’s upcoming wedding look, the stylist, who has been dressing her since she was 14, cheekily replied: “The wedding’s already happened. You missed it.”“It’s very true,” he added.He also told “Entertainment Tonight,” when asked by another reporter about Zendaya’s bridal look, “Y’all, the wedding already happened. Y’all missed it. The wedding’s over. Sorry.” He then proceeded to talk about all the movies the actress has coming out this year and the fashion choices and method dressing he has planned for those.Zendaya does have a busy year coming up. “Dune: Part Three”; “The Drama,” a romance co-starring Robert Pattinson in which she plays an engaged woman; the third and final season of “Euphoria”; Christopher Nolan’s upcoming “The Odyssey”; and a new “Spider Man” film are all set to release this year — the latter two with her beau.When asked about Zendaya’s wedding dress in an interview with Complex last year, Mr. Roach said, “It will probably be a wedding dress that nobody will ever see, to be quite honest. Because she and Tom are super private. There won’t be a Vogue spread, or there won’t be pictures of the wedding. And the people that she will invite will be really respectful of their privacy.”It seems like he was right. The two are famously private, with a similarly quiet engagement rollout last year. Speculation that the two stars were engaged began at the Golden Globe Awards in January 2025 when Zendaya, 29, was spotted wearing a rock on her left ring finger.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Sadiba Hasan reports on love and culture for the Styles section of The Times.AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
